{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_0c49381be0dffa50\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_0c49381be0dffa50/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"Response fetch failure in comparison view\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_bb78d680dd30a22ffa11cce1\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that both answer panes keep spinning when opening a comparison on RP-8073 and asks whether others see the same behavior.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908073.000029\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908073.000029\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A second tutor reports trying a second item and finding that the response still failed to appear.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908127.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U015\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908127.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks whether the failure happens before model responses are displayed.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908167.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908167.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"The team lead states that no model output was available to evaluate for the affected item.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908211.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908211.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"The team lead instructs the thread to mark the affected item as a response-fetch/tool incident and not invent a quality label. Verbatim quote: \\\"For the affected item, no model output was available to evaluate. Mark it as a response-fetch/tool incident and do not invent a quality label.\\\"\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908211.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908211.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"Current project instructions require recording a fetch incident when response panes never load and prohibit inferring response quality. Verbatim quote: \\\"If response panes never load, record a fetch incident and do not infer response quality.\\\"\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:36683c52\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The thread provides handling instructions but contains no report that response access recovered for either tutor.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908073.000029\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908127.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908167.000226\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908211.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908073.000029\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U015\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908127.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908211.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Two tutors report that responses fail to appear in comparisons, including spinning answer panes on RP-8073.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908073.000029\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908127.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908073.000029\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U015\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908127.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"The team lead instructed the thread to record the affected item as a response-fetch/tool incident without inventing a quality label; the thread does not report restored access.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908211.000339\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908073.000029\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908127.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908167.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908211.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908073.000029\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U015\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908127.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that both answer panes keep spinning when opening RP-8073; a second tutor reports that a response still failed to appear after trying a second item.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908073.000029\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908127.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908073.000029\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U015\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908127.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asked whether the failure happens before model responses are displayed.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908167.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908167.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d3\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The team lead stated that no model output was available to evaluate for the affected item.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908211.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908211.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d4\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"Current project instructions say to record a fetch incident when response panes never load and not infer response quality.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:36683c52\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action\", \"kind\": \"ACTION\", \"text\": \"Report a technical issue to engineering. Instruction: Report the response-loading failures to engineering, including RP-8073 and the second tutor's report, while retaining the existing fetch-incident handling. Draft to copy: Please investigate response-loading failures in this batch. Two tutors report responses failing to appear:\\n- A tutor reports that both answer panes keep spinning when opening comparison task RP-8073.\\n- A second tutor reports that a response still failed to appear after trying a second item.\\nFor the affected item, no model output was available to evaluate. It is being handled as a response-fetch/tool incident, without an invented quality label. Please check the loading behavior and advise on restoring access. Scope: This report concerns the reported loading failures; it does not establish a technical cause or extend the thread-specific instruction to unrelated incidents.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908073.000029\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908127.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908211.000339\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:36683c52\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908167.000226\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:rationale\", \"kind\": \"ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why this helps: The labeling instruction addresses classification, not restored access. Engineering can investigate the reported loading behavior while current guidance keeps missing output separate from response quality.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908073.000029\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908127.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908211.000339\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:36683c52\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908167.000226\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:need\", \"kind\": \"INTERVENTION_NEED\", \"text\": \"Why intervening now is needed (an operational problem that needs coordination): Two tutors report response-loading failures that prevent viewing the responses, and the thread supplies classification instructions without reporting restored access.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908073.000029\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908127.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908211.000339\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_bb78d680dd30a22ffa11cce1\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_bb78d680dd30a22ffa11cce1 is PARTIALLY_RESOLVED: The team lead settles the affected item's classification as a fetch/tool incident without a quality label. The complete thread contains no report that either tutor regained access to responses.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908073.000029\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908127.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908167.000226\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908211.000339\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:rationale\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Severity HIGH: Two distinct tutors report comparable failures to display responses, indicating disruption beyond one reporter; the team lead states that the affected item had no output to evaluate.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908073.000029\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908127.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908167.000226\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908211.000339\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:signal:HIGH[3]\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_SIGNAL\", \"text\": \"Rubric signal met - \\\"Multiple distinct people or affected tasks reporting a comparable problem within the relevant project, batch, and time window, suggesting broader disruption or systemic labeling risk. Consider the number affected relative to the known active group when that information is available; do not require an explicit statement of widespread impact\\\": Two tutors report responses failing to appear in the same thread, including spinning panes on RP-8073 and a failure after trying a second item.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908073.000029\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908127.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U010\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U010 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908073.000029\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U015\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U015 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908127.000113\"]}], \"member_threads\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908073.000029\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_bb78d680dd30a22ffa11cce1\", \"thread_id\": \"1790908073.000029\", \"author_id\": \"U010\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T02:27:53.000029Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U010\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Anyone else seeing this? Both answer panes keep spinning when I open a comparison. (task ref RP-8073)\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908127.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_bb78d680dd30a22ffa11cce1\", \"thread_id\": \"1790908073.000029\", \"author_id\": \"U015\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T02:28:47.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U010\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"I tried a second item and the response still failed to appear.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908167.000226\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_bb78d680dd30a22ffa11cce1\", \"thread_id\": \"1790908073.000029\", \"author_id\": \"U002\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T02:29:27.000226Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U010\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Does the failure happen before model responses are displayed?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790908211.000339\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_bb78d680dd30a22ffa11cce1\", \"thread_id\": \"1790908073.000029\", \"author_id\": \"U001\", \"author_role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T02:30:11.000339Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U010\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"For the affected item, no model output was available to evaluate. Mark it as a response-fetch/tool incident and do not invent a quality label.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"THREAD_SCOPE\"}], \"retrieved_sources\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:36683c52\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-instructions@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — Instructions (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Tool incidents and submission\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Tool incidents and submission\\nIf response panes never load, record a fetch incident and do not infer response quality. If Submit fails, capture the task ID, required-field state, error and exact button behavior. A selected label is not a completed submission until LT confirms it. Assess tool impact separately from the content rubric.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:4683724f\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Ties and preferences\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-05T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-05T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Ties and preferences\\n\\n### Q: How much improvement is needed to avoid a tie?\\nThe difference must offer a meaningful benefit to the user. Cosmetic phrasing alone usually does not. Explain that benefit; otherwise a tie can be appropriate.\\n\\n### Q: QA is reversing ties on similar pairs. What should I do?\\nShare the pairs, relevant prompt constraints and both rationales for calibration. Check whether the cases are actually comparable. An answer to one pair should not be generalized without matching its scope.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:47ed0c14\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-instructions@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — Instructions (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Instruction adherence versus accuracy\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Instruction adherence versus accuracy\\nScore these dimensions separately. An explicit required output structure, such as JSON, is not optional.\\n\\nThis guidance does not define a universal preference ordering for a response that is stronger on accuracy but weaker on a required format. When the applicable rules and actual pair do not settle the comparison, provide the exact prompt, 